{"kind":"request","text":"Hugh's explicit request, 2026-10-09: file a planner request for \"(1) the infrastructure for a durability-level choice when establishing acts.\" This is an implementation/planning request, not merely a design-only discussion.\n\nCONTEST-FIRST OBJECTIVE\nArtroom's primary goal is interaction around software development or equivalent processes for the Cloudflare demo competition. The demo must be compelling, demonstrate extraordinary flexibility/power of the fold-over-events application model, show more than one different application, and provide modern realtime multiuser responsiveness. Prioritize by contribution to winning the contest under the time constraint. Coordinate with the existing development/branch/review/publication work and the counting-demo companion request; avoid a general storage rewrite becoming the demo's critical path.\n\nREQUEST\nAssess, design and implement the smallest coherent infrastructure for choosing an act execution/durability contract when establishing the application/scope/act family, with shared application definitions, typed client/discovery/query/watch affordances and precise acknowledgments. Choose exact ownership, phases and scope according to planner judgment. Publish an updated dated design/implementation plan and deliver reviewed source slices and measured acceptance.\n\nRECONCILE EARLIER WORK\nExisting request 8a13f7b84eae5d2656a49352300fccf66696280f already requests a shared-language volatile-acts design note/plan, with URI correction. Responsiveness request db5384400f5916d929b37fa698d799a8fdce3af9 contains source-backed latency/query/Artifacts opportunities. Reconcile or amend existing owned slices; do not duplicate promises, conflict over common files, or run competing gates.\n\nAGREED SEMANTIC FRAME\nHugh simplifies policy to TWO questions:\n1. What must survive?\n2. Does confirmation wait for local application or JOURNAL COMMITMENT?\nA durability choice is valuable only if it functionally distinguishes cheap durability (scope/DO-backed journal, potentially asynchronous Git custody) from custodial durability (confirmation limited by Artifacts/other Git-store commitment). Do not multiply user-facing policy taxonomies or expose archive/publication machinery as unrelated knobs.\n- ONE combined volatile acts layer, encompassing presence, messaging and other temporary coordination, with ZERO durability guarantee and reset at any time. No separate signal-vs-act API. Initial definitions approximately Gitseq presence/attention-at-URI and messaging.\n- Cheap recorded durability preserves complete canonical acts, judgments and required evidence, commits them safely to existing DO SQLite and acknowledges at that commitment. Optional async Git storage/archive must not make the earlier acknowledgment falsely claim completed external custody.\n- Custodial durability must identify an actual authoritative/required journal commitment (e.g. authenticated Git sequence/ref advancement or required Artifacts custody). A queued/local provisional record cannot receive the final acknowledgment promised by that contract. DO/Git are not one atomic transaction; use explicit pending/unknown and exact-request reconciliation.\n- Actor-selected choice must be restricted to profiles legal for the established declared type/act family; never allow a caller to downgrade a review/authority/publication guarantee by passing ephemeral=true.\n- Artroom currently already journals ordinary acts before background Git operations. Optional Git publication is not by itself lower local durability. Git content publication still determines actual Merged/work-product completion.\n- If the full custodial-journal backend is too costly for the deadline, establish a sound interface and clearly unsupported boundary rather than false capability; prioritize the working profiles and measured benefit needed by the demo. Do not make multiple completed backends a prerequisite for realtime presence/counting.\n\nSHARED LANGUAGE AND GUARANTEES\nReuse items, typed fields, actor/session authority, guards, constraints, transitions, expected revisions, effects and timed semantics where valid. Define versioned execution/durability declarations/binding at establishment, separate from existing definition.profile rules-language version. Validate unsupported effects and retention/reference assumptions before use.\nSame scope can contain live interaction around recorded work, with explicit state/profile boundaries and independent live generation/revision versus durable fact/frontier. Applied live responses are generation-scoped, not durable FactRefs. Reset immediately after response is allowed.\nKeep mandatory identity/permission validation. Live references cannot become durable foreign facts without an explicit snapshot capture/new recorded act, current guards and retained evidence. Irreversible effects require durable operation identity/pre-send bookkeeping. Exclude them from the initial zero-durability profile unless a separate recorded boundary is invoked.\nPresence/message URI should primarily address existing scopes and their CONTENTS; inventory/reuse established address/reference forms, not a new arbitrary-topic namespace. Multiple actor sessions, leases, recipients and visibility remain explicit. Addressing attention is not confidentiality.\n\nGIT ROLES AND RETENTION\nThe design must handle Git as essential work product, system of record for definitions/roles, derived materialization, signed canonical log, or longitudinal archive without conflating them. Pin and retain rule/authority versions used by judgments. A Git materialization is disposable only if retained journal+recipe reconstruct it. DO history can be released only after complete verified custody and all recovery/provenance obligations are preserved; current checkpoints do NOT license history purging and replay currently starts at genesis. Do not implement checkpoint purging for the contest unless a small justified owned slice establishes the complete contract.\nGitless complete journals can preserve replay; current-state snapshots alone do not. Gitseq's current record identities already bind Git objects, so replacing its format is not implicitly in scope.\n\nIMPLEMENTATION PRIORITIES\n- Make ordinary interactions show known results promptly and refresh only affected views; authenticated notifications and automatic snapshot/watch synchronization, not manual refresh/full redraw.\n- Bounded view queries, in-flight read deduplication and lazy inspection; avoid serial all-lane/destination-history reconstruction on the response path.\n- Minimal volatile executor/session/generation/memory bounds and presence/messaging application definitions in the SAME syntax and common SDK.\n- Keep existing cheap durable judgment/commit/fold/evidence invariants intact.\n- Implement only needed custody policy/seam; use measured request/byte costs to select Artifacts native reads and immutable reuse.\n- Physical combining of scopes was discarded; no scope-merging project. Snapshot-only state mode is not an initial prerequisite.\n\nMEASUREMENTS AND THEIR LIMITS\nAt older deployed spike (not current platform), simple durable acts were68-73ms p50 and83-90ms p90; local SQLite transaction p50 was below timer resolution, max4ms. This does NOT measure a single-digit-ms production confirmation barrier. Source notes/2026-10-01-spike-room-core.md:92-108,149-160,264-277; land only recorded a head, did not pushmain.\nActual Artifacts rehearsal on2026-10-08: CLI comment0.6s, assignment0.5s, controlled merge3.6s, full edit/proposal/link/publication8.5s; /Users/hughpyle/tmp/artroom-rehearsal-1/transcript.md:164-225. These are individual whole-workflow timings, not isolated provider writes.\nCloudflare output gates delay outgoing responses until writes confirm; synchronous SQL execution is not the durability latency: https://blog.cloudflare.com/sqlite-in-durable-objects/ . Artifacts exposes push duration percentiles: https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/observability/metrics/ .\nCapture comparable volatile application, DO journal commitment and small Git custody timings on SAME deployment/connection, with p50/p95, cold/warm, response-path steps and peer-visible update. Suggested DEMO TARGETS, not current guarantees: prompt local feedback; same-geography ordinary peer updates ~150ms p95 and simple recorded acknowledgment ~200ms p95. Keep publication progress asynchronous without premature completion claims. Budget the measurement; no broad benchmark project.\n\nACCEPTANCE\nDeclared choice is discoverable and accurately determines what survives/when ack is valid. Live reset/epoch refs/session ownership/bounds/backpressure/lease behavior; recorded hashes/replay/grants/expected revisions unchanged; exact custody pending/unknown/lost reply and restart behavior; no silent weakened effects/cross-scope facts; snapshot/watch handoff and multiuser automatic updates; no high-rate live starvation of recorded work. Preserve source verification, authority, due transitions before judgment, durable attempts/recovery scheduling and actual publication confirmation.\nUse focused meaningful existing tests and one coordinated final gate per docs/testing.md; no mutation sweeps, blind repeated suites or competing gates. Report exact reviewed source, results, measured deltas, remaining unsupported choices and impact on contest/demo schedule.","body":{"conditions":"Assess and implement a coherent shared-language durability choice at act/scope/application establishment: zero-durability volatile local application, cheap DO-journal commitment, and accurately specified custodial journal commitment where supported. Reconcile existing design/responsiveness work; deliver bounded reviewed slices and measured realtime/commit behavior without broad backend redesign or weakening replay/custody guarantees.","priority_basis":"Contest-first: compelling multi-application realtime demo","target_head":"9d7e4c2777ea8d35441b4a9d79b407cd701065fa","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}